The Deep was a great god that once threatened the world, and was slain in part through the help of [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]]. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] says the name appears in no record he has seen.

On [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] the Deep was a great source of power believed to reside at the planet's core. It powered some of the more taboo spells there, and its followers were the largest of [[Org/Althane/The Mysteries|the Mysteries]]. Ingesting its blood, deepblood, brings on [[Phenomena/Althane/Sanguis Depsics|Sanguis Depsics]].

It has reached into [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]] from below. It broke the cognitive breakwater on the sixth floor, and where its touch falls people rise off the floor with mouths and eyes spilling yellow light, speaking together in one voice. They lunge at whatever comes near and burst when they strike.

It pressed on the mind of [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]], trying to drag him down into slumber, and where he was wounded his flesh closed under a black silk. When Karkov was killed the Deep would not let him go: a portal opened and eight fungal tendrils, like the [[Phenomena/Althane/Mycelia|mycelium]] seen in [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Vyre, the Inverted City|Vyre]], reached out and dragged what was left of his body through. The Deep does not suffer anyone to walk up to the portal it opens.

Its seat is the City of Yellow on [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]]: a hill of yellow buildings that move like creatures rather than stone, ringed by cloud that never quite parts, with a lake of black water at the centre and a lighthouse standing in it. Fungal tendrils wrap the lighthouse and find no way in. Karkov, remade in fungus and mindless, claws at its door.

By the reckoning of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] it is the strongest of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]], though long weakened. It speaks as hundreds of overlapping voices that do not resolve into meaning, and beneath them an intent can be felt. It wants into the lighthouse, and it offers to remake those who come to it into Thessians, the dynasty it calls the Thessians of Yord, and to rebuild the empire that was taken from it.
